instr:
Dimensionality reduction and regularized regression no longer work after the refactor

Our `@kanaries/ml` workflows used to reduce feature matrices, reconstruct them, and fit regularized regression models through the scikit-learn-style API. Please restore the missing implementations in `src/algebra/eigen.ts` and `src/algebra/lstsq.ts`, along with the models in `src/decomposition/pca.ts`, `src/decomposition/sparsePCA.ts`, `src/decomposition/truncatedSVD.ts`, `src/linear/elasticNet.ts`, `src/linear/lassoRegression.ts`, and `src/linear/ridgeRegression.ts`, so those workflows work again.

For example, reducing a matrix and mapping it back to the original feature space used to work like this:

```ts
import { Decomposition } from '@kanaries/ml';
const X = [[2, 1, 0], [4, 3, 1], [6, 2, 4], [8, 5, 3]];
const model = new Decomposition.PCA({ nComponents: 2 });
const reduced = model.fitTransform(X);
const reconstructed = model.inverseTransform(reduced);
console.log(reduced, reconstructed);
```

This should produce a reduced representation and a reconstruction in the original feature space; instead, constructing the model throws `not implemented`. The algebra utilities and the other models above also have throwing stubs. Use the API pages under `docs/content/docs/apis/decomposition/` and `docs/content/docs/apis/linear/` for algorithm behavior and option defaults, alongside the algebra doc comments. The `README.md` “Supported Algorithms” section lists the available models.

